Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation; provided, matters related to the introduction of the Senior Executive Service system among the provisions of Articles 7(1), 8(1), and 11(2), and the Appendix shall enter into force on July 1, 2006.
Article 2 (Transitional measure following abolition of organization regarding its public officials)
(1) If there is an incumbent corresponding to the prescribed number specified in the Appendix upon expiration of the time limit for activities of the Commission under Article 22, the prescribed number corresponding to such incumbent shall be deemed to separately exist until 1 year after termination of the activities of the Commission; provided, this shall not apply where the incumbent is a public official in extraordinary civil service.
(2) Among the prescribed number under paragraph (1), the prescribed number under Article 11(2) shall be deemed the prescribed number of public officials belonging to the relevant institution, and the remaining prescribed number shall be deemed the prescribed number of public officials belonging to the Ministry of the Interior and Safety. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008>

